chemtab for OS-9/68000======================ORIG holds comp.sources.misc volume 14, Chemtab 1.2 (three parts), asposted.  The files beside it build the OS-9 program.  looke.c is carriedacross parts 1 and 2 of the post and ORIG has it whole.What changed, and why:  tune.h       Under OSK the element list and the table outline are read               from /dd/LIB/chemtab, the transcript is printed with `lp',               and TRANSCRIPT -- a log of who ran the program -- is left               undefined, so no log is kept.  An include guard, because               Microware cpp warns at every repeated #define.  windows.h    Microware's curses.h has no include guard and every file               that includes windows.h has included curses.h already, so               under OSK windows.h does not include it a second time.  variables.h  The globals were defined in every file, which BSD's linker  element.h    merges and l68 rejects (and the copies came to more than  windows.h    64K of data).  Under OSK each set is declared extern except  main.c       in the one file that defines it: main.c for variables.h and  element.c    windows.h, element.c for element.h.  variables.h  getchar() in crmode is how chemtab reads a key.  Microware  scrmisc.c    stdio reads a terminal a line at a time, so under OSK               getchar() is chemtab_getc() in scrmisc.c: a character left in               stdin's buffer by scanf() or gets() first, otherwise one byte               read from the path.  main.c       SIGTSTP does not exist here and is not ignored.cleanup.c, dogph.c, esort.c, looke.c, ptabl.c, schar.c, vdata.c, graph.hand undefs.h build unchanged from ORIG.The title page's "\033#6" (double-width line) reaches the terminal with acursor movement inside it, so "#6" shows before the title.Data: LIB/chemtab/elist and LIB/chemtab/pertab.  The manual pages are inDOC/chemtab.Build: cc cleanup.c dogph.c element.c esort.c looke.c main.c ptabl.c          schar.c scrmisc.c vdata.c -DOSK -l=curses.l -l=termlib.l